# Project Scope

HOSSPI HMS frontend is the Flutter client for the full-stack hospital management system, implementing module workspaces, clinical and operational flows, and shared shell UI against the `hms-backend` API. Modules and boundaries: [`.cursor/app-write-up.mdc`](../../.cursor/app-write-up.mdc).

## Mandatory rules

- Must build production-ready module workspaces, not a generic disconnected starter.
- Must support Android, iOS, Web, Windows, macOS, and Linux where enabled; extra-small mobile through large desktop screens; smartwatch out of scope.
- Must integrate with `hms-backend` via repositories, DTOs, and [`.cursor/api-contract.mdc`](../../.cursor/api-contract.mdc).
- Should prefer Flutter SDK widgets, Material Design, and shared `lib/shared/` abstractions before custom frameworks or extra packages.
- Must avoid duplicate dependencies, folders, components, rules, and competing design systems.
- Module menus, routes, forms, actions, permissions, and visibility must match backend routes, permissions, entitlements, and APIs.
- Must reference entities by `human_friendly_id`; backend maps internal IDs.
- Must enforce RBAC+ABAC and subscription-package intersection ([`permissions.mdc`](./permissions.mdc)).

## Architecture invariants

- One architecture, one routing system (`go_router`), one state system (Riverpod), one design system, one shared component strategy.
- Mutation and reconciliation behavior is owned by [`instant_ui_sync.mdc`](./instant_ui_sync.mdc); layer boundaries by [`architecture.mdc`](./architecture.mdc). Must not override or restate them.

## Minimum runnable contract

- Startup: `main.dart`, `bootstrap.dart`, provider scope, predictable startup flow.
- Shell: `MaterialApp.router`, `go_router`, not-found route, responsive shell with menu bar and collapsible side nav.
- Theme: Material 3 light/dark/system with shared tokens.
- State: Riverpod providers with override-ready boundaries.
- Localization: English ARB baseline, `l10n.yaml`, generated l10n.
- Components: shared buttons, fields, dialogs, state views, layout helpers.
- Workspaces: `AppWorkspace` + `AppListTable` ([`ui-workspace.mdc`](./ui-workspace.mdc)).
- Quality: format, analyze, tests, CI commands.

